WEBVTT

00:01.420 --> 00:05.670
When I got home from school, there were shoes there,
other than my family's...

00:06.000 --> 00:10.420
And they were... I realized immediately
that those were Yuri-san's...

00:10.790 --> 00:14.420
But at that time, I couldn't care less,
what people would say about me and...

00:14.750 --> 00:16.540
I headed to my big brother's room and...

00:16.540 --> 00:18.750
I didn't even knock, and I opened the door...

00:19.880 --> 00:20.880
And then...!

00:21.210 --> 00:22.250
"And then..."!?

00:22.460 --> 00:23.920
A-and then...!

00:24.330 --> 00:29.330
And then, Yu... Yuri-san was hunched
over my big brother and...

00:30.330 --> 00:31.580
She was kissing him...!

00:33.420 --> 00:37.580
Wh-whoa!

00:52.040 --> 00:56.000
<b>The Dreaming Boy</b>

00:52.040 --> 00:56.000
<b>is a Realist</b>

00:56.130 --> 01:01.710
With a command from the sky that's peeking out,
we hold onto our feelings as we depart

01:01.710 --> 01:06.460
Even though our eyes meet,
we're swayed by the wind into a roundabout way

01:07.540 --> 01:13.000
A dream snapshot taken by the blink of the eyes;
the memories adorn my heart

01:13.000 --> 01:18.420
It seems I like these times; even though they're frustrating

01:19.460 --> 01:24.330
Staying away then getting closer; a dream I'd started to give up on

01:24.580 --> 01:30.000
The day I can land that well; I want to try chasing after that

01:30.000 --> 01:35.420
The sky is filled up with the things that can't be all conveyed

01:35.580 --> 01:41.210
For some reason, the change in countenance
of your true feelings was at odds

01:41.210 --> 01:49.540
Even though I might get lost, the sky always had two heartbeats

01:49.540 --> 01:52.040
I've told you many times

01:52.210 --> 01:58.210
If these youthful feelings are joined together,
I wonder what kind of view will spread out

01:58.210 --> 02:02.880
I want to know that colorful feeling

02:09.500 --> 02:11.210
So, basically, this is how things are.

02:09.710 --> 02:12.670
<b>Coffee. With a Ratio to Milk About 8 to 2. Sugar 1 Teaspoon, Caramel Powder Too, Please.</b>

02:11.210 --> 02:14.500
It's become difficult for Ichinose-san
to face her older brother,

02:14.710 --> 02:18.040
and since things can't keep going on like this,
with a feeling that she had to do something about this,

02:18.040 --> 02:20.500
she came to work part-time at this used bookstore.

02:21.000 --> 02:21.920
<b>Ichinose</b>

02:21.000 --> 02:21.920
<b>In training</b>

02:21.420 --> 02:25.540
She wants to be affectionate with the big brother
she loves, but she can't since he has a girlfriend now,

02:25.540 --> 02:27.670
so she has no choice but to detach
herself from her older brother.

02:28.290 --> 02:31.040
So then, in order to also nurture
that spirit of independence,

02:31.040 --> 02:35.290
there was no way she could just easily
quit the part-time job, and that's how it is.

02:36.330 --> 02:37.250
I understand now.

02:37.250 --> 02:37.920
Oh!

02:37.920 --> 02:40.250
That Ichinose-san, you have the resolve.

02:40.710 --> 02:42.540
Well then, let's do our best, okay?

02:44.380 --> 02:45.040
Yes!

02:45.540 --> 02:48.540
<b>We buy</b>

02:45.540 --> 02:48.540
<b>used books.</b>

02:46.630 --> 02:48.920
Ever since then, when it comes
to Ichinose-san's working manner...

02:49.130 --> 02:51.000
That has really been amazing.

02:52.580 --> 02:56.420
Maybe for Ichinose-san, yesterday's events turned
into a sort of expression of determination,

02:56.830 --> 02:58.790
so she's overflowing with motivation.

02:59.710 --> 03:00.540
Alright!

03:01.500 --> 03:06.080
One often hears stories that you fill up that void in
your heart when you get hurt, by working, you know?

03:07.000 --> 03:10.380
Well, although the stories I know
are from like dramas and mangas.

03:12.460 --> 03:13.960
I will do that!

03:14.080 --> 03:15.540
Oh, thank you.

03:17.380 --> 03:20.540
I kind of feel there's a sense of coordination
that's developed with Ichinose-san.

03:20.920 --> 03:22.040
And as I expected, what's left is...

03:22.330 --> 03:23.580
Dealing with customers, huh?

03:24.420 --> 03:25.830
"Dealing with customers"...?

03:25.830 --> 03:27.670
Oh, did I say that out loud?

03:28.670 --> 03:33.210
Well, if any customers of a certain type come,
I'll handle them, so first of all, why don't you watch?

03:33.500 --> 03:35.080
Oh, a customer-

03:35.080 --> 03:35.580
What?

03:35.580 --> 03:36.540
Welcome-

03:36.540 --> 03:38.460
U-um...

03:39.130 --> 03:40.790
Welcome, Sasaki-san.

03:42.670 --> 03:45.080
Ichinose-san, this is Sasaki-san.

03:45.420 --> 03:48.420
You might not believe it, but she is a middle schooler.

03:48.420 --> 03:50.790
Huh!? A middle schooler?

03:51.460 --> 03:53.710
Sasaki-san, this is Ichinose-san.

03:54.000 --> 03:56.710
She is a new part-time worker, and she is my classmate.

03:57.250 --> 03:59.540
So, you are a classmate of Sajo-san?

03:59.830 --> 04:02.460
Pleased to meet you. Ichinose-senpai.

04:02.460 --> 04:08.460
Oh... U-um... Nice to meet you... Kouhai.

04:08.460 --> 04:09.250
Huh?

04:13.250 --> 04:18.040
As Sasaki-san has come for the first time in a while,
this would be where I'd like to have a leisurely chat,

04:18.330 --> 04:21.670
but to be honest, right now I might be
at my limit just dealing with Ichinose-san.

04:21.920 --> 04:23.080
No, wait a sec...

04:23.460 --> 04:26.460
Sasaki-san, you might get along well with Ichinose-san.

04:26.750 --> 04:28.540
Ichinose-san is an avid reader too.

04:28.540 --> 04:29.080
What!?

04:30.040 --> 04:35.040
Is that so? I do not have any reading companions
around me, so that makes me happy.

04:35.040 --> 04:36.630
I hope we can be good friends, please.

04:36.790 --> 04:39.290
Oh... I do read books, but...

04:39.290 --> 04:39.960
Wow...

04:39.960 --> 04:44.000
Sasaki-san looks happy. Maybe this
won't end up in an awkward atmosphere?

04:44.170 --> 04:46.830
U-um... Right now, I'm working, so...

04:46.830 --> 04:48.330
Oh, my apologies.

04:48.330 --> 04:49.380
No, it's okay.

04:50.250 --> 04:52.500
As long as you can switch back when a customer comes.

04:53.500 --> 04:57.000
Um, Ichinose-senpai, what kind of books do you read?

04:57.830 --> 05:00.290
I don't have any particular preferences.

05:00.290 --> 05:02.500
If I'm attracted by the title or the book cover, then...

05:02.670 --> 05:07.250
Wow! That is wonderful.
So, you love "books" themselves, right!?

05:07.500 --> 05:08.750
That is cool!

05:09.250 --> 05:12.790
Um, what is your favorite author? Your favorite genre?

05:13.210 --> 05:15.880
You just said you do not have any preferences, but...

05:13.460 --> 05:15.670
I'm going to go organize some books.

05:15.880 --> 05:18.960
For example, what kind of titles or letters are you attracted to?

05:21.920 --> 05:25.540
Ichinose-senpai, about how long
does it take you to read one book?

05:25.880 --> 05:27.210
It depends on the book...

05:27.460 --> 05:31.130
I understand. It may be too good that
you purposely spread it across some days,

05:31.130 --> 05:33.380
or you are curious about what is ahead,
so you read it right away.

05:33.670 --> 05:35.460
Do you have any recommendations?

05:35.460 --> 05:36.080
Oh!

05:38.130 --> 05:43.250
After all, doesn't it feel a little special, if it is
a recommendation from a person who loves books?

05:43.460 --> 05:44.960
Well, that's true...

05:45.250 --> 05:49.080
I'm glad. Ichinose-san seems kind
of passive, but she's talking, so...

05:47.210 --> 05:48.920
Like this book.

05:48.920 --> 05:53.420
I read it before and it was really interesting, so I recommend it.

05:53.750 --> 05:59.040
But customers aren't coming, and at this rate,
Ichinose-san can't practice dealing with customers-

05:53.750 --> 05:57.750
Wow! Alright! Thank you very much!

06:02.330 --> 06:05.710
Alright, we're starting the role playing.
This is a simulation of dealing with customers.

06:05.710 --> 06:06.420
Uh-oh...

06:06.420 --> 06:09.080
You can do it. You can do it. Ichinose-senpai!

06:09.380 --> 06:11.460
Doesn't this place have magazines?

06:11.460 --> 06:14.080
Oh! W-we don't carry them.

06:14.500 --> 06:16.580
Huh? Why don't you carry them?

06:16.960 --> 06:18.250
Wh-why...?

06:18.790 --> 06:21.670
Oh! I-I will go ask the owner.

06:22.460 --> 06:26.880
Alright, that's one possible way of handling this.
By the way, as a different countermeasure-

06:28.210 --> 06:29.420
Where did she go?

06:29.580 --> 06:31.580
No way. Did she really go see the old guy!?

06:31.580 --> 06:33.170
Oh... Huh...

06:36.330 --> 06:37.210
Way to go!

06:37.210 --> 06:38.540
Keep it up!

06:39.670 --> 06:40.670
I'm sorry...

06:41.080 --> 06:43.790
It's fine. Plus, the owner was in a good mood too.

06:44.460 --> 06:47.750
Wow...! So, this is a part-time job...

06:48.630 --> 06:53.880
Okay then, next is Sasaki-san's turn. Can I count on
you as the role of a seemingly troublesome customer?

06:54.130 --> 06:58.960
Yes! You can count on me. This is also a step towards
adulthood! It is learning about the real world!

07:00.790 --> 07:01.710
Lucky...

07:06.130 --> 07:08.880
Don't worry, it's good that everyone is different!

07:09.080 --> 07:10.750
H-here I come!

07:11.330 --> 07:15.080
Yo, yo, yo! Hey! You bastard!

07:17.790 --> 07:18.830
Thanks, yo!

07:19.880 --> 07:22.000
That's a troublesome customer
with eccentric preferences.

07:22.750 --> 07:24.330
Thank you very much.

07:27.420 --> 07:28.580
I will come again.

07:28.830 --> 07:33.500
Oh, Ichinose-senpai! I will read the book
you recommended by the next time.

07:33.630 --> 07:36.250
Huh? Oh, that's not...

07:38.500 --> 07:40.790
She's like a lily of the valley, swaying in the wind...

07:42.460 --> 07:44.750
You know, no one came besides Sasaki-san today.

07:45.290 --> 07:46.540
There are days like this too.

07:46.830 --> 07:47.920
Oh, okay...

07:48.500 --> 07:50.630
She's a girl with that kind of vibe,
but I hope you'll be friends.

07:50.630 --> 07:53.210
Even when I quit, I'm glad it looks
like you'll be able to talk to her.

07:53.210 --> 07:53.750
What!?

07:54.000 --> 07:55.330
Are you quitting?

07:55.630 --> 08:00.080
What? It's because I'm quitting that there was a
recruitment for a new part-timer. You didn't know that?

08:00.580 --> 08:01.290
Yeah...

08:01.830 --> 08:05.330
Well, as you can see, this store doesn't
need two people, you know?

08:05.920 --> 08:09.790
So, well, Ichinose-san, I don't know if I can serve your
purpose,

08:09.790 --> 08:12.000
but I hope you'll let me keep being a senpai until I quit.

08:12.630 --> 08:14.250
Thank you very much.

08:15.330 --> 08:17.250
I'm going to go organize the shelves.

08:18.000 --> 08:19.380
Huh? Okay.

08:20.920 --> 08:22.580
It's almost time to get off work, huh?

08:30.960 --> 08:32.790
Once summer break is over...

08:32.790 --> 08:36.130
I'll probably become estranged
from Ichinose-san again.

08:37.670 --> 08:41.460
But why did Ichinose-san talk
to me about something like that?

08:42.330 --> 08:43.210
<b>Milk</b>

08:50.540 --> 08:51.080
Huh?

08:51.460 --> 09:01.330
<b>Sajo, Aika, K</b>

08:51.460 --> 08:57.000
<b>How was it, with the part-timer girl?</b>

08:53.080 --> 08:57.000
<b>I listened to her. It seems like</b>

08:53.080 --> 08:57.000
<b>she wants to become independent.</b>

08:55.080 --> 08:57.000
<b>Is it that serious for her?</b>

08:57.000 --> 09:00.000
<b>I listened to her. It seems like</b>

08:57.000 --> 09:00.000
<b>she wants to become independent.</b>

08:57.000 --> 09:00.000
<b>Is it that serious for her?</b>

08:57.080 --> 09:00.000
<b>Aika</b>

08:57.080 --> 09:00.000
<b>She wouldn't think of wanting to</b>

08:57.090 --> 09:00.000
<b>become independent, unless it was</b>

08:57.090 --> 09:00.000
<b>something really serious, I think.</b>

09:00.000 --> 09:01.330
<b>Is it that serious for her?</b>

09:00.000 --> 09:01.330
<b>Aika</b>

09:00.000 --> 09:01.330
<b>She wouldn't think of wanting to</b>

09:00.000 --> 09:01.330
<b>become independent, unless it was</b>

09:00.000 --> 09:01.330
<b>something really serious, I think.</b>

09:00.080 --> 09:01.330
<b>That's true.</b>

09:02.290 --> 09:04.080
Oh, you're here?

09:08.750 --> 09:15.330
Coffee. With a ratio to milk about 8 to 2.
Sugar 1 teaspoon, caramel powder too, please.

09:15.580 --> 09:16.920
Could you give me a minute?

09:17.170 --> 09:18.460
It's gonna take that long?

09:18.710 --> 09:19.830
I'm on it, ASAP.

09:31.750 --> 09:32.330
Huh?

09:33.630 --> 09:35.630
<b>Sajo, Aika, K</b>

09:33.630 --> 09:35.630
<b>Once school starts again,</b>

09:33.630 --> 09:35.630
<b>let us know in detail, okay?</b>

09:36.130 --> 09:37.790
Un-der-stood.

09:38.880 --> 09:44.380
I see. The reason why Ichinose-san talked to me was
because "there's no other person she can talk to."

09:45.250 --> 09:47.330
When she's at school, she's always by herself, and...

09:47.920 --> 09:48.750
Even at home too.

09:49.880 --> 09:51.380
<b>Aika</b>

09:49.880 --> 09:51.380
<b>It's a promise!!</b>

09:51.960 --> 09:54.920
If Ichinose-san had even one girl
that she was friendly with, then...

09:55.420 --> 09:58.960
I probably wouldn't have ever heard from her,
about her situation.

09:59.790 --> 10:00.830
Is it ready yet?

10:00.830 --> 10:01.880
Yeah, coming right up.

10:01.880 --> 10:04.790
Honestly, you shouldn't keep a customer waiting.

10:06.250 --> 10:07.710
Sorry to keep you waiting.

10:08.670 --> 10:09.630
Jeez...

10:18.710 --> 10:20.540
Hey, did something happen?

10:20.540 --> 10:22.380
Huh? No, not particularly.

10:22.380 --> 10:23.380
Uh-huh...

10:24.420 --> 10:25.040
Huh?

10:29.580 --> 10:31.460
Hey! You not gonna have anymore!?

10:34.420 --> 10:35.830
Bleh! Yuck!

10:36.210 --> 10:36.920
Huh!?

10:41.670 --> 10:43.380
<b>We buy</b>

10:41.670 --> 10:43.380
<b>used books.</b>

10:47.790 --> 10:50.500
You don't have to overextend yourself
and carry the same amount that I do.

10:50.830 --> 10:51.960
Let's do things leisurely.

10:51.960 --> 10:54.000
Oh... Thank you very much.

10:55.210 --> 10:56.000
Here.

10:56.000 --> 10:56.920
O-okay.

10:57.330 --> 10:58.170
Oomph!

10:58.960 --> 11:01.830
It really just looks like an elementary schooler
is doing her best, to me.

11:02.420 --> 11:03.540
Welcome!

11:04.170 --> 11:05.830
Yeah. That was good just now.

11:09.040 --> 11:11.380
<b>The Feeling of Eggs</b>

11:16.880 --> 11:18.130
<b>Everyday Pasta</b>

11:16.880 --> 11:17.500
<b>The Feeling of Eggs</b>

11:17.250 --> 11:18.130
<b>Everyday Omelets</b>

11:23.040 --> 11:23.880
Big Brother...

11:28.210 --> 11:29.250
Hello.

11:29.630 --> 11:32.830
Yuri-chan says she'll make omelet rice for us.

11:32.830 --> 11:35.580
Oh, Mina-chan, would you like to eat with us too?

11:35.580 --> 11:36.920
Huh!? Oh...

11:37.080 --> 11:39.630
Yuri-chan, I'm looking forward to your cooking.

11:39.630 --> 11:42.330
Leave it to me! It's my number one dish that I cook best!

11:42.330 --> 11:43.420
I'm looking forward to it!

11:44.420 --> 11:46.830
Wow! Mine has a heart on it!

11:51.380 --> 11:54.380
Yeah! Success! How about the taste?

12:06.460 --> 12:07.210
Mina?

12:10.630 --> 12:11.630
U-um...

12:11.790 --> 12:12.500
Huh?

12:12.960 --> 12:14.750
It's about this, and...

12:13.040 --> 12:14.880
<b>Devoted to used books.</b>

12:13.040 --> 12:14.880
<b>Hamaminami Book Store</b>

12:15.130 --> 12:15.830
Oh.

12:16.420 --> 12:17.420
For this...

12:17.630 --> 12:20.040
You do it like this, and then, like this.

12:20.420 --> 12:21.630
I will give it a try.

12:22.210 --> 12:23.460
Like this, and then...

12:25.000 --> 12:25.750
Like this.

12:26.170 --> 12:30.710
Perfect. Speaking of, Ichinose-san, you totally
handle books with care, you know?

12:30.710 --> 12:31.540
What...?

12:31.920 --> 12:33.210
You see, for me, at the beginning,

12:33.210 --> 12:36.920
it had to be hammered in that I needed to be
more careful with the handling of merchandise.

12:37.330 --> 12:38.500
So, I think that's awesome.

12:38.500 --> 12:40.170
Y-you think so...?

12:40.170 --> 12:41.670
Yeah, I admire that.

12:43.580 --> 12:44.830
Wh-what is it?

12:45.250 --> 12:49.170
Ichinose-san, I think it's better if you let
your face show like that on a regular basis.

12:50.290 --> 12:53.920
Oh! Crap. Why am I saying something
that sounds like I'm hitting on her?

12:53.920 --> 12:54.540
Huh?

12:54.920 --> 12:55.750
Oh! Nothing!

12:57.830 --> 12:59.880
Y-you think so...?

12:59.880 --> 13:01.580
S-so cute!

13:01.750 --> 13:03.130
<b>Devoted to used books.</b>

13:01.750 --> 13:03.130
<b>Hamaminami Book Store</b>

13:04.540 --> 13:05.500
For that...

13:05.920 --> 13:08.330
Huh? I'm sorry, what was that...?

13:08.750 --> 13:10.170
Oh, nothing.

13:13.630 --> 13:15.750
I'll be retiring soon, huh?

13:16.790 --> 13:21.000
But with this, I should be able to greet
the new school term without reserve.

13:26.580 --> 13:28.130
Um, excuse me.

13:29.210 --> 13:30.080
Yes?

13:31.920 --> 13:34.670
Teddy bear-senpai! Hang on, that means...

13:36.500 --> 13:37.290
Mina!

13:42.040 --> 13:46.040
<b>The Dreaming Boy</b>

13:42.040 --> 13:46.040
<b>is a Realist</b>

13:46.040 --> 13:50.540
<b>Hamaminami Book Store</b>

13:46.040 --> 13:50.540
<b>Used books -</b>

13:46.040 --> 13:50.540
<b>Buy & Sell</b>

13:46.040 --> 13:50.540
<b>We buy</b>

13:46.040 --> 13:50.540
<b>used books.</b>

13:47.080 --> 13:50.460
So, this is where you were.
I had a hard time tracking you down.

13:50.920 --> 13:53.330
And it seems like you swore mom to secrecy too.

13:53.790 --> 13:56.290
This is perfect timing. Are you getting off work right now?

13:56.290 --> 13:58.290
Why don't we go eat out for a change together-

13:58.290 --> 13:59.670
Oh! No!

13:59.880 --> 14:00.750
Mina!?

14:01.380 --> 14:03.000
I'm sorry, you are...?

14:03.460 --> 14:05.000
Oh, my name is Sajo.

14:05.330 --> 14:08.960
I have a senpai-kouhai relationship
to your younger sister here.

14:09.210 --> 14:11.710
I mean, but at school, we are classmates.

14:12.080 --> 14:15.170
It is not like I have that kind of relationship
to your younger sister at all.

14:15.170 --> 14:18.540
I'm sorry, Sajo-kun, would you mind
just moving out of the way?

14:18.540 --> 14:19.540
Oh, sure.

14:20.580 --> 14:21.670
Ichinose-san?

14:22.420 --> 14:23.790
She's totally looking at me!

14:24.130 --> 14:25.960
No, hang on, Wataru Sajo.

14:26.250 --> 14:28.630
Why did Ichinose-san hide behind me?

14:27.880 --> 14:29.000
It's my fault.

14:29.420 --> 14:31.880
Who is the one that I should be supporting?

14:29.420 --> 14:32.460
I didn't think about your feelings, Mina. I'm sorry.

14:33.250 --> 14:36.130
Um, shouldn't we move over to a cool place?

14:36.420 --> 14:37.880
Now is not the time for something like-

14:37.880 --> 14:38.880
For your younger sister.

14:39.130 --> 14:41.960
Are you sure you want her to continue being
exposed under the blazing sun like this?

14:43.790 --> 14:44.750
All right.

14:45.130 --> 14:47.130
<b>Hamaminami Book Store</b>

14:45.130 --> 14:47.130
<b>We buy</b>

14:45.130 --> 14:47.130
<b>used books.</b>

14:45.580 --> 14:47.790
There is a place right over there where we can relax, so...

14:50.380 --> 14:51.880
<b>Notice of the available hours for the eat-in space.</b>

14:58.130 --> 14:59.040
Senpai.

14:59.330 --> 15:00.750
Please use this.

15:01.040 --> 15:02.670
Oh, thanks.

15:03.460 --> 15:04.630
It's hot, isn't it!?

15:05.750 --> 15:10.000
I'm sorry, Sajo-kun. I was lacking
a little in cool headedness earlier.

15:10.460 --> 15:12.380
Not at all, please don't worry about it.

15:17.080 --> 15:19.080
Mina. I'm sorry.

15:22.380 --> 15:23.880
Um, Ichinose-san.

15:24.540 --> 15:28.750
Oh, do you know the reason why your younger sister
began doing a part-time job?

15:29.040 --> 15:33.040
I didn't hear it directly from her,
so I don't know exactly why, but the gist of it, yes.

15:33.130 --> 15:36.290
What? By any chance, have you two
not been on speaking terms this whole time?

15:37.460 --> 15:38.750
I see.

15:40.920 --> 15:43.330
Mina. Will you please listen to me?

15:48.500 --> 15:50.080
What is it, Big Brother?

15:52.630 --> 15:57.040
It's my fault that I ended up neglecting you
after I started going out with Yuri-chan.

15:57.500 --> 16:01.330
Like before, let's cuddle and read books together.
Let's snooze together.

16:01.750 --> 16:05.460
Oh... But that's Yuri-san's spot now, so...

16:05.630 --> 16:07.960
Yuri-chan wouldn't butt into stuff like that.

16:07.960 --> 16:10.460
But I feel bad for Yuri-san, so...!

16:10.580 --> 16:14.330
There's no need to worry about that.
Yuri-chan is a kind person.

16:14.710 --> 16:16.920
Could you please understand that, Mina?

16:17.880 --> 16:19.500
Sorry to keep you waiting, Ichinose-kun!

16:19.670 --> 16:21.380
C'mon, you gotta be kidding me.

16:21.710 --> 16:23.710
Yuri-chan. You came.

16:23.710 --> 16:28.250
Yeah. Since I don't think this is an issue
that's just between Ichinose-kun and Mina-san.

16:28.250 --> 16:29.130
Um...?

16:29.460 --> 16:32.750
My name is Sajo. I'm in the same
part-time job and school with her.

16:33.000 --> 16:35.130
Yuri Hanaoka. Nice to meet you.

16:39.380 --> 16:40.040
There.

16:41.750 --> 16:43.920
It's been a while, Mina-san.

16:43.920 --> 16:45.170
Y-yes...

16:45.170 --> 16:47.920
I heard you suddenly started a part-time job.

16:48.170 --> 16:51.250
And together with Ichinose-kun, we were wondering why.

16:51.830 --> 16:53.460
But I was told the inside story and...

16:54.000 --> 16:55.000
I'm sorry.

16:55.460 --> 16:57.960
It's because I stepped into the spot that was yours.

16:59.790 --> 17:03.540
Mina-san, based on your personality,
a part-time job is difficult, right?

17:04.960 --> 17:07.210
I think it's too soon for you.

17:08.210 --> 17:10.250
I-it is not too soon for me!

17:10.670 --> 17:13.330
Mina, why are you being that stubborn?

17:13.580 --> 17:16.500
Up until now, you were never like that,
not even once, you know?

17:16.500 --> 17:20.420
I also don't want to break Ichinose-kun's family
apart because of something like this.

17:20.790 --> 17:22.330
Please come back.

17:28.830 --> 17:33.330
Um, could the two of you listen to what
Ichinose-san has to say, a little bit more?

17:33.330 --> 17:34.170
What?

17:34.420 --> 17:38.460
Ichinose-san is doing a great job.
And her work is proactive too.

17:38.960 --> 17:40.170
"Proactive"?

17:40.630 --> 17:42.330
So, this is what I think, but...

17:42.670 --> 17:46.500
For you two senpai to go out together, and
you ending up treating your younger sister offhandedly;

17:47.040 --> 17:50.330
and for your younger sister to use that as
an opportunity to detach herself form her older brother;

17:51.080 --> 17:53.330
either one of those are natural things
that happen, aren't they?

17:53.330 --> 17:59.250
Well, that may be true, but... Mina is a shy girl,
so she must be forcing herself to do so.

17:59.250 --> 18:03.420
That's right. It's because
we're really thinking about Mina-san that-

18:03.420 --> 18:08.000
Senpais, just how old do you
think Ichinose-san is right now?

18:08.290 --> 18:09.130
What...?

18:09.630 --> 18:14.750
In a real sense, Ichinose-san chose this path
in order to congratulate the two of you.

18:15.420 --> 18:18.630
Are you intending to take away
that opportunity from Ichinose-san?

18:19.130 --> 18:20.670
That wasn't my intention.

18:20.790 --> 18:24.500
Senpai, I am not going to be the one to say that
you have to detach yourself from your younger sister.

18:24.500 --> 18:30.290
However, to think "it's to be expected that my younger
sister will always be by my side," is wrong, isn't it?

18:31.250 --> 18:33.080
If a younger sister detaches herself
from an older brother,

18:33.080 --> 18:34.880
does that mean everyone can't laugh together anymore?

18:35.170 --> 18:36.210
That's not how it is, is it?

18:38.420 --> 18:42.420
As a senpai of her part-time job,
who has observed her from close by, if you ask me...

18:42.960 --> 18:47.080
Deciding Ichinose-san's future is
something you should probably wait,

18:47.080 --> 18:50.540
until Ichinose-san can explain in her own words, right?

18:58.540 --> 19:00.790
For the time being, I think I was able
to buy you some time.

19:01.580 --> 19:03.630
Yes. Thank you very much.

19:05.460 --> 19:06.250
What's up?

19:06.250 --> 19:09.580
U-um, wasn't I wrong...?

19:09.580 --> 19:10.330
What?

19:10.630 --> 19:13.460
You always correct me when I make a mistake, so...

19:14.960 --> 19:17.380
Well, you know, this isn't during our part-time job.

19:17.790 --> 19:21.710
As to whether or not you're right or wrong,
isn't it okay as long as you know?

19:22.080 --> 19:22.790
What...?

19:23.080 --> 19:25.330
You see, I've been thinking about
this ever since we came here.

19:25.750 --> 19:27.960
I don't know about other
people's family situations and...

19:28.330 --> 19:32.210
In that case, as I am your senpai of
your part-time job, based on what I've seen,

19:32.210 --> 19:33.790
is how I decided I'd make a judgement.

19:34.580 --> 19:37.880
Ichinose-san, your big brother and
others came to take you back.

19:38.290 --> 19:41.710
For the people around you, maybe that seems right.

19:42.460 --> 19:45.040
But you know, if that's the case, then Ichinose-san,

19:45.040 --> 19:47.750
for what reason did you keep doing
your best at your part-time job, up until now?

19:48.250 --> 19:50.170
You got reprimanded by unreasonable customers and...

19:50.580 --> 19:51.420
You apologized and...

19:52.000 --> 19:55.630
Even for things that you weren't good at,
Ichinose-san, you overcame them one by one.

19:56.380 --> 19:57.920
I've continued to watch you the whole time.

19:58.170 --> 20:01.540
<b>In training</b>

19:58.170 --> 20:01.540
<b>Ichinose</b>

19:58.460 --> 20:01.130
Ichinose-san, you have unquestionably
continued to do your best.

20:02.540 --> 20:06.290
And if all of that came to nothing,
there's no way I would've been okay with that, you know?

20:09.880 --> 20:10.540
What!?

20:10.750 --> 20:13.380
Oh! I mean...! Uh...

20:14.540 --> 20:16.540
<b>School visit tour</b>

20:14.540 --> 20:16.540
<b>Orientation meeting</b>

20:14.540 --> 20:16.540
<b>Assembly hall is this way.</b>

20:17.250 --> 20:18.210
Morning.

20:19.330 --> 20:21.040
Natsukawa, it's been a while.

20:21.420 --> 20:23.920
Huh? Did you change something about yourself?

20:23.920 --> 20:26.830
I got a little tan and maybe gained some muscle.

20:27.630 --> 20:29.330
You see, I've been running outside this whole time.

20:29.580 --> 20:32.580
I see. It does seem like the athletic club is busy.

20:32.790 --> 20:36.580
Yeah. Natsukawa, did you go
anywhere for the summer break?

20:36.710 --> 20:40.210
<b>*When there are questions, what is okay to answer.</b>

20:36.710 --> 20:40.210
<b>Correct things based on fact.</b>

20:36.710 --> 20:40.210
<b>Correct things for school services.</b>

20:36.710 --> 20:40.210
<b>Example: School events.</b>

20:36.710 --> 20:40.210
<b>Facts based on your experiences</b>

20:36.710 --> 20:40.210
<b>(Convey those are only your experiences.)</b>

20:36.710 --> 20:40.210
<b>*Things you should not answer lightly.</b>

20:36.710 --> 20:40.210
<b>Things related to sense of values.</b>

20:36.720 --> 20:40.210
<b>Do not force your ideas onto others.</b>

20:40.670 --> 20:43.080
I'll go get stuff, so go ahead and take a seat.

20:45.960 --> 20:46.670
<b>Sajo, Aika, K</b>

20:45.960 --> 20:46.670
<b>You have a new message.</b>

20:46.670 --> 20:48.210
<b>Sajo, Aika, K</b>

20:46.670 --> 20:48.210
<b>I want to go again, okay!?</b>

20:46.670 --> 20:48.210
<b>Sajo</b>

20:46.670 --> 20:48.210
<b>Bring me along too, okay?</b>

20:46.670 --> 20:48.210
<b>What should we do next?</b>

20:46.670 --> 20:48.210
<b>Sajo</b>

20:46.670 --> 20:48.210
<b>I have to get a swimsuit ready.</b>

20:46.670 --> 20:48.210
<b>Hmm.</b>

20:46.670 --> 20:48.210
<b>Next is beach volleyball.</b>

20:49.500 --> 20:50.540
Sorry to keep you waiting.

20:53.130 --> 20:55.000
Th... Thanks.

20:59.920 --> 21:00.630
Huh?

21:01.250 --> 21:03.170
What is it, Sasaki-kun?

21:03.540 --> 21:05.460
Oh, no, it's nothing.

21:05.750 --> 21:07.500
Huh? Okay.

21:26.580 --> 21:29.040
So annoying! Or so it seems, right?

21:29.330 --> 21:32.580
Aw! I wish I hadn't said that...

21:33.420 --> 21:39.540
But you know, why're you suddenly making
that curt face towards me...?

21:41.250 --> 21:43.460
A text that's been left on read and abandoned

21:43.460 --> 21:45.750
But there are replies if it’s a group text, kind of thing

21:45.960 --> 21:47.920
I thought we were close, but then you became distant

21:48.170 --> 21:49.710
Why am I this lonely?

21:49.710 --> 21:51.580
You're not going to chase after me, today?

21:51.580 --> 21:53.170
I wish I could be honest with myself

21:54.630 --> 22:00.960
That's because it's the first time
I learned there's such a heartrending feeling...

22:00.960 --> 22:02.380
And yet, hey!

22:02.380 --> 22:03.920
Why're you going away??

22:03.920 --> 22:05.670
Why is it a secret!?

22:05.880 --> 22:08.040
I'm full of frustration and...

22:08.040 --> 22:09.420
Oh! Oh!

22:09.420 --> 22:11.130
I can't say something like this

22:11.130 --> 22:15.080
But earlier those weren't my true feelings

22:15.080 --> 22:16.460
Let that get through to you

22:16.540 --> 22:18.170
Why do I get angry...?

22:18.170 --> 22:19.710
I can't be cute...

22:19.710 --> 22:22.170
You don't like me anymore...??

22:22.330 --> 22:25.040
Oh! Oh! Oh, oh!

22:27.040 --> 22:28.000
Why?

22:28.670 --> 22:29.960
Don't hate me

22:33.000 --> 22:34.420
...Listen, "You see...!"

22:39.040 --> 22:41.210
<b>We buy</b>

22:39.040 --> 22:41.210
<b>used books.</b>

22:41.830 --> 22:43.380
Morning, Ichinose-san.

22:43.830 --> 22:44.460
Huh?

22:44.460 --> 22:45.670
<b>In training</b>

22:44.460 --> 22:45.670
<b>Ichinose</b>

22:44.670 --> 22:46.920
Wh-what do you think...?

22:47.920 --> 22:48.830
I like it!

22:53.290 --> 22:54.380
Hello!

22:55.500 --> 22:58.170
I have come again, Ichinose-senpai!

22:58.460 --> 22:59.880
For you too, Sajo-san!

22:59.880 --> 23:00.710
Welcome.

23:01.170 --> 23:03.790
I read the book you told me about, from the other day.

23:03.920 --> 23:05.380
What!? Already?

23:05.540 --> 23:09.000
Yes! I was mesmerized by
that strawberry tart tactic at the end!

23:09.460 --> 23:12.330
It was unexpected that the pastry chef
was that evil of a person.

23:12.670 --> 23:17.250
I get that! The superb foreshadowing and
the catchy subject matter were very good, you know?

23:17.250 --> 23:18.500
We're in the middle of work right now.

23:18.500 --> 23:19.130
Oh!

23:19.130 --> 23:23.500
I am sorry! It is so fun to talk to Ichinose-senpai,
that I couldn't help myself.

23:23.710 --> 23:24.630
I'm sorry.

23:24.830 --> 23:25.750
Ichinose-san.

23:26.960 --> 23:28.330
What day is today?

23:28.330 --> 23:30.080
T-today...?

23:30.880 --> 23:32.420
Training period is finished.

23:33.000 --> 23:33.500
<b>In training</b>

23:33.630 --> 23:34.500
Congratulations.
